A circuit breaker is a stateful guard around a dependency. It differs from retry. Its state determines whether a dependency call is attempted. Threshold accounting must match the actual implementation.

> calls to the circuit breaker fail immediately, without any attempt to execute the real operation.

Source: [Q06](/lore/durability-bibliography#q06); [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it), [B11](/lore/durability-bibliography#b11-property-based-testing).

## Failure it prevents

Callers keep spending capacity on a known-unhealthy dependency.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

No dependency circuit-breaker API was found. Compose timeout and typed failure handling with an explicit XState lifecycle. Define whether state is local or shared.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Effect.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Schema.ts`.

## How to check

Generate success, failure, timeout, cooldown, and probe histories. Verify exact threshold semantics and visible state changes. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Bulkheads isolate scarce capacity](/lore/bulkheads-isolate-capacity), [Supervision chooses what restarts](/lore/supervision-is-a-recovery-policy).

Connect this to [the existing rat-stack guidance](/lore/lifecycles-are-machines).

